---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero';
---

<Layout title="Frequently Asked Questions" description="Answers to common questions about booking, provider verification, pricing, and how AZAP works.">
    <PageHero 
        client:load
        title="Common Questions." 
        subtitle="Booking, pricing, vetting, and what happens if something goes wrong."
    />
    
    <section class="py-16 md:py-24 px-6">
        <div class="container-tight max-w-3xl !px-0">
            <div class="space-y-3">
                {[
                  {
                    q: "How much does it cost to book?",
                    a: "Nothing. Booking is free and AZAP adds nothing to your bill. You agree a price directly with your pro and pay them directly. We take no commission on the job, so nobody has to inflate their quote to cover us."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "How fast can I get a pro?",
                    a: "We aim to call you back within 15 minutes of your booking, and we\u2019ll tell you honestly on that call when someone can reach you. Arrival time depends on the job and who is free. We would rather give you a real time than a promise we cannot keep."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "How do you vet your pros?",
                    a: "Four checks before anyone can take a job: their National Identity Number with the document, a bank account in their own name, a named guarantor we contact by phone, and a photograph so you know who is arriving. We also meet every pro in person before adding them."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "How do I pay?",
                    a: "Directly to your pro, in cash or by bank transfer, once the work is done. AZAP never holds your money and never takes a cut of it. You pay exactly what you agreed with them, and nothing to us."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "Who decides the price?",
                    a: "You and your pro do. They look at the job and quote you. That matters, because nobody can honestly price a leak before seeing it. If you are not happy with the quote you are free to say no, and it costs you nothing."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "What if I need to cancel or reschedule?",
                    a: "Call or message us and we will sort it. There is no cancellation fee. If you cancel after a pro has already set off, please let us know as soon as you can, because they have made the journey."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "What if something goes wrong?",
                    a: "Tell us. We call every customer after the job to check it went well, and we keep a record of every booking: who was sent, when they arrived, and what was agreed. If there is a problem you have a real person to take it up with. That is the thing you do not get finding someone through a WhatsApp group."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "Where do you operate?",
                    a: "Enugu, for now. We open one neighbourhood at a time on purpose: a vetted pro twenty minutes away is worth more than a thousand spread thinly across the country. If you are somewhere else, leave your email on our homepage and we will tell you when we reach you."
                  },
                  {
                    q: "Do I need the app?",
                    a: "No. Everything happens through this website and a phone call. The AZAP app is coming, and when it does you will be able to track your pro on a map and confirm arrival with a PIN, but nothing about booking today depends on it."
                  }
                ].map((faq, i) => (
                    /* An accordion, not fifteen open cards.
                       Expanded, this page ran to 6.6 screens on a phone, and
                       nobody reads every answer — they arrive with one question.
                       The first is open so the pattern is obvious without a tap.

                       <details> rather than JavaScript: it works with none, is
                       keyboard operable, and announces its own state. Every
                       answer stays in the HTML, so search engines and in-page
                       find still see all of it. */
                    <details open={i === 0} class="faq-item card-enterprise px-6 py-1 md:px-10">
                        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left md:py-6">
                            <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-xl">{faq.q}</h2>
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="faq-chevron h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-zinc-400 transition-transform" aria-hidden="true">
                                <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6" />
                            </svg>
                        </summary>
                        <p class="pb-6 pr-9 text-base font-medium leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">{faq.a}</p>
                    </details>
                ))}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
